laurel 2905: USB poll period, TX queue, ENDTRANSFER at bus reset (ports of the poll part of negroni 0361, the USB
part of 0382 and the reset part of 0366).

- ud_thread polled every 1 ms with the default timer leeway: one frame per poll and direction (about 1 MB/s).
  Now: frames in the last 2 s or a TX in flight/queued: every laurelusb_pollus (200 us, no leeway);
  configured and idle: laurelusb_idle_ms (4 ms); no host configured: laurelusb_nohost_ms (20 ms). Every
  controller event and every queued frame (ud_if_output wakes the thread) returns to the fast poll. Raw mode
  (before the ue0 attach) and the timer-call service keep 1 ms.
- TX queue 32 -> 128 frames (a full queue drops frames and TCP backs off).
- Bus reset: ENDTRANSFER + FORCERM on every active data transfer (RX, TX, notification) before the data
  endpoints go off (Linux dwc3_stop_active_transfers). Kill switch laurelusb_resetend=0. (The 0282 part, data
  endpoints dropped until SET_CONFIGURATION, was already in laurel 2005.)
- Status line counts polls; line "LAUREL USB POLL: on: 200 us while frames move, 4 ms idle, 20 ms without a host,
  TX queue 128, ENDTRANSFER at bus reset on". The old poll: laurelusb_pollus=1000 laurelusb_idle_ms=1.
- Not ported: the 0361 RX ring / TX batch (new DMA layout) and the 0366 soft-reconnect watchdog.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
